{
  "_schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "section",
  "slug": "properties-panel",
  "label": "Properties panel",
  "description": "The right column of an item page: a completion meter, then a Properties / People / Suggestions tab set, with Properties as a long label-and-control form.",
  "role": "aside",
  "apps": [
    "studio"
  ],
  "patterns": [
    "asset-detail-360"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "properties",
    "completion",
    "aside"
  ],
  "derivedFrom": {
    "surface": "Studio > Catalog > Dataset > General",
    "capturedOn": "2026-09-30",
    "productVersion": "manufacturing.zeenea.app/studio"
  },
  "slots": {
    "completion": "'Completion Level' heading over a progress bar that prints its percent once.",
    "tabs": "Properties, People, Suggestions, with the suggestion count after the label.",
    "form": "The item type's properties in its template's groups (upper-case group headings such as DATA Contract and OUTPUT PORT), each a label over its control: single and multiple selects, text fields, date fields, and 'Add <property>' on an empty select; then Source properties as 'label : value' pairs."
  },
  "renderNotes": [
    "Parameter, filled by the page that splices it: completion_percent (a number, no % sign: progress-bar-small prints the sign).",
    "The form is the captured Dataset's (manufacturing.zeenea.app, 2026-09-30): DATA Contract (4 properties), OUTPUT PORT (5), the first three of Cataloging, then Source properties. The product's form continues below the fold: the rest of Cataloging (Layer, Sensitivity, Approval Status, Market study, Stage, Personally Identifiable Information, Retention period) and GOVERNANCE (Complaints, Data Quality, Data Sampling, Topic_select).",
    "A date property is `calendar` carrying the property name as its own Label: calendar prints \"Date\" when its Label is empty, so it cannot take a sibling TEXT label as the other controls do. Every other control takes Label \"\" beside a TEXT label.",
    "A multiple select's values are one comma list in `Value`; the product draws each as a removable chip, dropdown-select-default draws the list as text. Option emoji the tenant sets (the hourglass on In Progress) are the tenant's data and are left out."
  ],
